{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"ac77b06139b92ab3","name":"card_event_battery","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/WorldAtWar/events/card_event_battery","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"BATTERY","text":"Deal 4 damage to target unit, excess damage is dealt to the enemy HQ.","flavorText":"An artillery battery is a grouping of artillery, mortars, rocket artillery, multiple rocket launchers, and in later years surface-to-surface missiles, ballistic missiles, cruise missiles, and other weapons designed to improve command and control of gunnery crews and their systems. General Patton often commented that the US artillery won the war for them, and one example of its importance was during the Battle of the Bulge. Due to bad weather Allied air superiority was out of the picture, which meant that the artillery had to fill the void. The US Army managed to amass around 350 guns of all calibers in the northern sector of the Bulge which was one of the largest concentrations of artillery in history. This massive firepower helped slow down the German advance and proved vital in the Allied defense of Elsenborn Ridge and Bastogne.","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_battery","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_battery_title","SourceString":"BATTERY","LocalizedString":"BATTERY"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_battery_text","SourceString":"Deal 4 damage to target unit, excess damage is dealt to the enemy HQ.","LocalizedString":"Deal 4 damage to target unit, excess damage is dealt to the enemy HQ."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_battery_history","SourceString":"An artillery battery is a grouping of artillery, mortars, rocket artillery, multiple rocket launchers, and in later years surface-to-surface missiles, ballistic missiles, cruise missiles, and other weapons designed to improve command and control of gunnery crews and their systems. General Patton often commented that the US artillery won the war for them, and one example of its importance was during the Battle of the Bulge. Due to bad weather Allied air superiority was out of the picture, which meant that the artillery had to fill the void. The US Army managed to amass around 350 guns of all calibers in the northern sector of the Bulge which was one of the largest concentrations of artillery in history. This massive firepower helped slow down the German advance and proved vital in the Allied defense of Elsenborn Ridge and Bastogne.","LocalizedString":"An artillery battery is a grouping of artillery, mortars, rocket artillery, multiple rocket launchers, and in later years surface-to-surface missiles, ballistic missiles, cruise missiles, and other weapons designed to improve command and control of gunnery crews and their systems. General Patton often commented that the US artillery won the war for them, and one example of its importance was during the Battle of the Bulge. Due to bad weather Allied air superiority was out of the picture, which meant that the artillery had to fill the void. The US Army managed to amass around 350 guns of all calibers in the northern sector of the Bulge which was one of the largest concentrations of artillery in history. This massive firepower helped slow down the German advance and proved vital in the Allied defense of Elsenborn Ridge and Bastogne."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WorldAtWar","isReserved":true,"draftBaseWeight":0.9,"receivedAbilitiesFromCards":[{"Key":"excess","Value":{"CardsGivingAbility":[0]}}],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'TACTICAL_AIRSTRIKE_17'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/OrdersFeb17/TACTICAL_AIRSTRIKE_17.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/t_battery